(package nx/tactics/decks/place
 :libs (lib base :path nx/tactics/base)
 :doc "places")

(func placemap-tactics : base/placemap
 [tactics : base/tactics]
 (base/placemap<-placelist
  (base/place
   :name "Aaru"
   :titles "Field of Reeds"
   :summary
    "The realm of Aegytan dead spirits")
  (base/place
   :name "Air Field"
   :image "images/cards/place-airfield.svg"
   :summary
    "* May [Deploy] Aircraft
     * Repairs Aircraft
     * Required to extend Aircraft Range")
  (base/place
   :name "Amber Realms"
   :titles "Amber Space, Crytalline Space, Geometric Space"
   :summary
    "* Amber Space - The expansion phase of the multiverse near the beginning of spacetime. Space and time are still forming, entropy has just been created, and order rules. Real space exists but order tends to crytallize and calcify existence.
     * Denizens - [Leviathan], [Weaver]"
  (base/place
   :name "Angular"
   :titles "Angular Space, Angular Time, Point Time, Tindalos"
   :summary
    "* Angular time - An eternal moment after [Creation], before expansion. Space and time had not yet formed. No matter, no curves, no time. Only intense energy, eternally reflected back upon itself. Ultimate power. Ultimate Order. Forever.
     * Denizens - [Hounds of Tindalos], [Langoliers], [Norns], [Radiance]. The beings if you can call them that are pure energy that know only Order. Mindless and infallible. Drawn across spacetime like electric current to 'correct' disorders in time.")
  (base/place
   :name "Astral"
   :titles "Astral Plane, Astral Realm, Complex Space, Dream, Hyperreal, Hyperspace, I-Space, Imaginary Realm, Imaginary Space, Luminal Realm, Overrealms, Possibility, Positive Space, Probability, Reason Realm, Science, Subjective Reality, Sublime, Superspace, Superreal, The Pale, Ultrareal, Ultraspace"
   :reference
    "* Astral - Of the Stars
     * Ad Astra - To the Stars
     * Though the story is fictional, as far as the characters are concerned, their fate is real. Therein lies the rub, are you and I the audience? Or characters on the stage? Nobody can know for sure. Afterall, nothing is easier to fool than the senses. - Furina, Genshin Impact"
   :summary
    "* The Astral Realm is the realm of the Mind and of possibilities. It connects all of the upper realms, and some believe all realms are birthed from the infinite potential of the Astral.
     * Layers - The Astral is a continuous space but is logically divided into sections:
     ** [Angular] - The 'moment' of Angular time before spacetime exists
     ** [Amber Realms] - Realms are frozen in rigid order.
     ** [Celestial] - Realms conform to the rules of a clear mind
     ** [Periphery] - The mind realms nearest the [Material]
     ** [Firmament] - The barrier between the Astral and Material
     * Description - The realm appears as a dense starfield filled with a glowing fog and motes of crackling energy called Luminaries (Tachyons). Touching a luminary fills one with energy and inspiration, but contacting too many too quickly will overload the body in a violent explosion.
     * Transition - When entering the Imaginary Realm, there is a sudden, frightening sensation of flipping forward and sideways at once and then it is over.
     * Speed - In the Imaginary Realm, the speed of light is the lowest speed that an object can move. Due to relativity, the speed of light is effectively zero speed. Here physical objects move at wildly accelerated speeds and can easily become lost or destroyed in the insane speeds and energies of this Realm.
     * Mind and Will - Everyone seems to experience the Imaginary Realm differently with many experiencing wild and terrible hallicinations. Those entering this Realm with just their minds find that their abilities are vastly increased. They are filled with a sense of power and appear massive in this realm, dwarfing stars. They appear as an idealized version of themselves with Body equal to Mind and all abilities may use Mind instead.
     * Body - Physical rules barely apply. Resistences use Mind instead of Body.")
